name issue_536_reverse_outage_45s
describe forward link healthy, feedback path down for 45 s (asymmetric path failure): video waits in the pacer and A/V sync drags audio
# #536 (Tester's rev_outage.scn, comment of 2026-10-29): with no feedback for 45 s the target falls by RTT backoff,
# video waits in the pacer and A/V sync drags audio to ~2 s mouth-to-ear. Yardstick #792 (#724) ran it on both
# stacks, 10 seeds: every cell is in the parity band (#725), and libwebrtc M157 does the same (m2e p95 2070 vs ours
# 2059 ms, pacer p95 2245 vs 2244 ms, target 656 vs 657 kbps). So these lines sit at libwebrtc's worst seed in 1-10
# (#729); the Tester's stage-2 targets (m2e < 400, video e2e < 1000) are the `stage:later` item #795, not suite lines.
compare_seeds 10
seed 1
duration 120s
at 0s capacity=1000kbps delay=40ms queue=300ms
reverse at 0s delay=40ms
reverse at 20s down
reverse at 65s up
# libwebrtc seeds 1-10 (#792): 2039 2044 2087 2043 2085 2063 2095 2077 2105 2063 (worst 2105). Ours seed 1: 2044.
expect audio.mouth_to_ear_p95_ms < 2106
# libwebrtc: 0.04 0.05 0.06 0.05 0.02 0.08 0.08 0.09 0.09 0 (worst 0.09); no interruptions. Ours seed 1: 0.04, 0.
expect audio.concealed_pct < 0.1
expect audio.interruptions == 0
# libwebrtc: 2288 2306 2330 2293 2281 2304 2359 2326 2300 2281 (worst 2359). Ours seed 1: 2288.
expect video.e2e_delay_p95_ms < 2359
# libwebrtc: 1620 1575 1603 1549 1418 1685 1626 1561 1720 1594 (worst 1720). Ours seed 1: 1612.
expect sync.av_offset_p95_ms < 1721
# libwebrtc: freezes 0 0 1 0 0 1 1 0 1 0 (worst 1); longest 29 27 226 3 34 223 206 31 234 13 (worst 234). Ours seed 1: 0, 26.
expect video.freeze_count <= 1
expect video.longest_freeze_ms <= 234
# libwebrtc: 27.49-27.62 (worst 27.49). Ours seed 1: 27.56.
expect video.render_fps > 27.4
# libwebrtc: 0 on every seed. Ours seed 1: 0.
expect video.keyframe_requests == 0
# libwebrtc: utilization 60.85-61.56 % (worst 60.85), queue p95 34.7-45.3 ms (worst 45.3). Ours seed 1: 62.0, 42.3.
expect cc.utilization_pct > 60.8
# #738 (needs the window's sign-off, program.md 0.2 "Guard rails during a port"): with GoogCC's cwnd_reduce_ratio taken
# after the minimum clamp, as libwebrtc, seed 1's queue p95 is 48.7 ms, over libwebrtc's worst seed 45.3. On seeds 1-10:
# ours 48.7 42.3 51.5 39.9 39.5 43.2 49.3 44.3 39.6 40.4 (mean 43.9; main 41.5), libwebrtc 37.4 42.0 45.3 41.5 42.7 41.5
# 42.9 34.7 36.7 41.6 (mean 40.6, sd 3.3): in the parity band. Video e2e p95 moves closer per seed (mean 2304 vs 2307).
# #777 (needs the window's sign-off, program.md 0.2 "Guard rails during a port"): with the NACK's report blocks
# not counting the packet that revealed the gap, as libwebrtc, seed 1's queue p95 is 52.2 ms. Seeds 1-10: ours
# 52.2 42.3 46.6 41.4 39.5 42.3 48.6 46.6 39.6 40.4 (mean 44.0; main 43.9), libwebrtc 37.4 42.0 45.3 41.5 42.7
# 41.5 42.9 34.7 36.7 41.6 (mean 40.6): the mean doesn't move. The line goes to ours seed 1, above
# libwebrtc's worst seed (45.3), for the window to judge.
expect cc.queue_p95_ms < 52.3
